  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Cascara — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Cascara.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Cascara.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Cascara"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Cascara" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #E5DBDA   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #010000   crema     — primary text (15.46:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #006262   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #E5DBDA   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #C9B1AF   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #010000   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #010000   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #B4001B   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #DCCDCB   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #006262   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #DCCDCB   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #B4001B   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #144904   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #7D4E00   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #015D8A   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #4C1D80   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #006262   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #130504   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #674E4C   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #B4001B   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #195C02   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #705300   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #015D8A   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #480381   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #006262   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #006262;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #010000   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
